15 PFTs
9  Stage PFTs
5  Live Pools
5  Phenology Stages
*******************************************************************************************************
                    Stage-Based Phenology Parameter Definitions and Units
                   ------------------------------------------------------
                                     1   Leaf-Out
                                     2   Growth
                                     3   Mature
                                     4   Stress
                                     5   Dormant
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
LP=Leaf Pool
FR=Fine Root Pool
CR=Coarse Root Pool
WP=Stem/Wood Pool
PP=Product Pool

-----Growing Season Start Parameters (FlagG)------
DayMinI = Minimum light to start growing season for increasing day lengths (hr)
DayOffD = Parameter to start growing season for decreasing day lengths (hr)
          > 0: Offset from maximum day length
	  < 0: Daylength threshold to restrict day lengths (winter wheat)
TAWMin  = Minimum fraction of total available water (TAW) in
            top three layers to start growing season (-)
TAWLen  = Number of sequential days TAW_FTop > FlagG_WMin (days)
TempMin = Minimum temperature to start growing season (K)
TempLen = Number of sequential days temperature > FlagG_Tmin (days)

-----Growing Season Reset Parameters (FlagA) -----
ALen   = Running-mean length for Assim_Mean (days)
AReset = Threshold value for FAssim to set FlagA

-----Phenology Factor Parameters-----
Day Length Potential-----
PSD_Ref  = Phenology daylength potential reference daylength (hr)
PSD_Mul  = Phenology daylength potential daily change (-)
PSD_Min  = Phenology daylength potential minimum (-)

Growth Potential (calculates climatological suitability, climp)---------
ClimP_A   = ClimP exponential adjustment coefficient
ClimP_B   = ClimP exponential adjustment base
ClimP_C   = ClimP multplicative adjustment coefficient
ClimP_D   = ClimP multplicative adjustment offset
ClimP_Min = ClimP minimum value
ClimP_Max = ClimP maximum value
CWA_Type = Water availability type:
        1 = CUPR Precipitation
	2 = Total Precipitation
	3 = PAWFRW
	4 = TAWFRW

CLAI_Coef = Climp coefficient for climatological reference LAI (Clim_LAI)
CLAI_OffL = Lower offset for minimum Clim_LAI
CLAI_OffG = Higher offset for maximum Clim_LAI
PSG_Min  = Minimum value for phenology growth potential

Weather Potential--------
PSW_Type = Water availability type for phenology weather potential:
           1=PAW_FTOP;            2=PAWFZW;  3=2*PAW_FALL;
           4=PAW_FALL>0. ==> 1.;  5=TAW_FTOP;  6=TAWFZW
           7=RSTFAC2;             8=RSTFAC4;   9=PAWFRW
PSW_RML  = Phenology weather potential running-mean length (days)

Phenology Stage Index--------
Thr = Min/Max threshold between stages


-----Vegetation Phenology-Dependent Parameters-----
-----(per stage)-----------------------------------
LP_Alloc=Leaf pool allocation fraction (-)
FR_Alloc=Fine root allocation fraction (-)
CR_Alloc=Coarse root allocation fraction (-)
WP_Alloc=Stem/Wood allocation fraction (-)
PP_Alloc=Product allocation fraction (-)
M_Adj=Adjust allocation fractions from moisture rules?
T_Adj=Adjust allocation fractions from temperature rules?

LP_Trans=Leaf pool transfer fraction (-)

VMAX = Rubisco velocity of sun leaf per phenology stage (mol/m2/s)
VMAX_CA = Calirbation ratio between VMAX and Carbonic Anhydrase velocity (-)

*********************************************************************************************************

